WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.640
Could this growing business survive an unexpected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:07.680
tragedy? Ten Thirty One Productions started&nbsp;
off strong, but where is the company today?

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.880
On "Shark Tank," most pitches fall into familiar&nbsp;
categories, like household goods, technology,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.160
childcare products, or food. It's relatively&nbsp;
rare for the sharks to consider pitches in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:21.640
entertainment realm. Yes, there have been a&nbsp;
few exceptions, like the inclusivity-oriented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:26.440
comics company Black Sands Productions. There's&nbsp;
also Drive Suits' robotic car-themed strolling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:31.520
performance venture. However, companies like Ten&nbsp;
Thirty One Productions are a relative anomaly.

00:00:31.641 --> 00:00:33.961
The brainchild of entrepreneur Melissa Carbone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.961 --> 00:00:38.240
Ten Thirty One Productions began as a company&nbsp;
that stages live horror-themed events. Their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:42.240
most popular attraction is the Los Angeles&nbsp;
Haunted Hayride — a terrifying nighttime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.040
trip through several scary tableaus set&nbsp;
up in the city's famed Griffith Park.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:49.600
Carbone and her business partner and&nbsp;
ex-spouse Alyson Richards launched&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.440
Ten Thirty One Productions in 2009.&nbsp;
By the time of her "Shark Tank" pitch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.200
Ten Thirty One Productions' most lucrative&nbsp;
revenue stream came from the Haunted Hayride.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:02.080
Each October, the Haunted Hayride was operational&nbsp;
for the 17 days leading up to Halloween. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:07.520
consistently sold out, adding up to about&nbsp;
$1.8 million in revenue in that period alone.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:12.400
Carbone went into the tank to pitch her company&nbsp;
in October 2013, with her episode airing six days&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:16.800
before Halloween. She asked for $2 million&nbsp;
in exchange for a 10% equity stake in her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.560
company. Kevin O'Leary and Robert Herjavek&nbsp;
didn't believe in her financial projections&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.720
for the following year, while Lori Greiner&nbsp;
didn't consider the investment worth her time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:30.320
so all three bowed out. Daymond John offered $2&nbsp;
million for 40%, but when Carbone countered with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.040
the same dollar amount for 20%, Mark Cuban&nbsp;
swooped in and took the deal. And with that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.476
it was his biggest investment in&nbsp;
his first five seasons on the show.

00:01:38.476 --> 00:01:40.613
"Everywhere I go there's zombies."

00:01:40.613 --> 00:01:45.040
Ten Thirty One had big plans for expansion,&nbsp;
including a New York-based haunted hayride,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:50.360
as well as a "Great Horror Campout" — an immersive&nbsp;
12-hour camp-a-thon filled with scares. Bigger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:55.280
picture, Carbone wanted to have a Ten Thirty&nbsp;
One attraction in every major city in the U.S.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:59.000
The first New York Haunted Hayride&nbsp;
was a success. In its first year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:03.640
it made 36% more than its Los Angeles&nbsp;
counterpart's second-year performance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:08.440
even if bad weather meant that it fell short of&nbsp;
its $5 million goal. This, along with Cuban's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:13.800
investment, allowed Ten Thirty One to branch&nbsp;
out. As of May 2015, it offered two hayrides,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.200
the camping attraction, a haunted cruise called&nbsp;
the "Ghost Ship," several Great Horror Movie Night&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.840
outings, and even a film production company that&nbsp;
aimed to make movies related to its attractions.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:27.440
The popularity of Ten Thirty One Productions and&nbsp;
its numerous affiliated attractions has turned it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:31.840
into one of the biggest "Shark Tank" success&nbsp;
stories out there. Of course, not every big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:36.320
leap of faith that Mark Cuban or any of the other&nbsp;
Sharks have taken on an investment deal has turned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:41.240
out so rosy, so it's worth looking closer at how&nbsp;
everything came together in this unique case.

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:46.080
As touched upon prior, Ten Thirty One Productions&nbsp;
was actually doing quite well even before it got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:50.640
featured on "Shark Tank." Between having several&nbsp;
established brands and a solid stream of revenue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:55.800
the business was in no need of a savior. Melissa&nbsp;
Carbone told Dread Central in a 2017 interview,

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:00.080
"We were doing really well and I had little to&nbsp;
no interest in selling a piece of the company.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:03.760
I recognized what the platform 'Shark&nbsp;
Tank' could provide so I reconsidered."

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.520
Indeed, arguably the greatest&nbsp;
effect of Cuban's involvement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:09.520
with Ten Thirty One Productions is&nbsp;
how it allowed the venture to carry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:13.920
out its pre-existing plans for expansion more&nbsp;
efficiently. In the interview, Carbone noted,

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.560
"The amount of time that opportunity&nbsp;
saves us on sourcing location, scouting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:20.880
and partnerships has been incredible.&nbsp;
It took a year to permit a location&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:24.840
for our first attraction and once we&nbsp;
became known and associated with Mark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:28.840
everyone in the country with a piece of land&nbsp;
or building to offer had us on speed dial."

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:30.760
It seems that Ten Thirty One Productions was bound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:33.800
for success regardless of whether it&nbsp;
obtained a deal on "Shark Tank" or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:38.280
not. Unfortunately, not everything was&nbsp;
smooth sailing for the growing company.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:41.600
The New York Post reported that&nbsp;
back in 2016, one of the Haunted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:45.880
Hayride set pieces — supposedly a&nbsp;
fog machine — fell on a customer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:51.560
leaving them severely injured. This led&nbsp;
to a lawsuit in 2018, and as a result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:56.280
Carbone sold Ten Thirty One to event company&nbsp;
Thirteenth Floor Entertainment Group. With that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.280 --> 00:04:00.301
said, she is still actively operating her&nbsp;
rides and events through the new company.

